# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize {#step-2-optimize}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize {#step-2-optimize}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We optimize details associated with the circuit to be run, the observable to be measured, and the noise-learning parameters. As a starting point, we select the least-busy Heron processor and instantiate it with fractional gates turned on. These fractional gates allow for greater sensitivity in some of our post-selection filtering.\n"
msgstr "Ino-optimize natin ang mga detalyeng kaugnay ng circuit na tatakbuhin, ang observable na susukatin, at ang mga noise-learning parameters. Bilang panimulang punto, pinipili natin ang least-busy Heron processor at ino-instantiate ito na naka-on ang fractional gates. Ang mga fractional gates na ito ay nagbibigay ng mas malaking sensitivity sa ilan sa ating post-selection filtering.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we will transpile our circuit to ISA instructions, [as required for execution on our QPUs](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture). The choice of physical qubits to run on has a large impact on the quality of the results, because coherence times and gate fidelities vary across a device and drift over time. For a careful experiment, it can pay off to hand-select a chain of qubits informed by quick benchmarking experiments (see, for example, the [Real-time benchmarking for qubit selection](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) tutorial). For the purposes of this tutorial, we rely on the Qiskit transpiler to select a layout based on the backend's coupling map and its most recent calibration data.\n"
msgstr "Una, i-transpile natin ang ating circuit sa ISA instructions, [na kailangan para sa execution sa ating mga QPU](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture). Ang pagpili ng physical qubits na patatakbuhan ay may malaking epekto sa kalidad ng mga resulta, dahil ang coherence times at gate fidelities ay nag-iiba sa buong device at nagbabago sa paglipas ng panahon. Para sa isang maingat na eksperimento, maaaring makatulong ang manu-manong pagpili ng chain ng qubits base sa mabilis na benchmarking experiments (tingnan halimbawa, ang [Real-time benchmarking for qubit selection](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) tutorial). Para sa layunin ng tutorial na ito, umaasa tayo sa Qiskit transpiler para pumili ng layout base sa coupling map ng backend at sa pinakabagong calibration data nito.\n"

