# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. Tighten forward bounds with quantum speed limits {#b-tighten-forward-bounds-with-quantum-speed-limits}"
msgstr "b. Tighten forward bounds with quantum speed limits {#b-tighten-forward-bounds-with-quantum-speed-limits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next tighten the bounds by using the `tighten_with_speed_limit` function. The geometric spread of the observable's lightcone is already fully accounted for in the forward bounds computed above. What this function adds is a self-consistency pass that leverages the limited speed at which information can flow through the circuit &mdash; the lightcone grows by at most one qubit per layer of two-qubit gates &mdash; to tighten the previously computed bounds with respect to each other. The information flows in both directions:\n"
msgstr "Sa susunod, hinihigpitan natin ang bounds gamit ang `tighten_with_speed_limit` function. Ang geometric spread ng lightcone ng observable ay ganap nang naisaalang-alang sa forward bounds na nakalkula sa itaas. Ang idinaragdag ng function na ito ay isang self-consistency pass na kumukuha ng ideya mula sa limitadong bilis kung saan makakadaan ang impormasyon sa circuit &mdash; lumalaki ang lightcone ng hindi hihigit sa isang qubit kada layer ng two-qubit gates &mdash; upang higpitan ang dati nang nakalkulang bounds kaugnay ng isa't isa. Dumadaloy ang impormasyon sa dalawang direksyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the commutator bounds to the bounds on the backpropagated observable: if the observable commutes with a $Z$ error on a qubit, then it cannot have much $X$ or $Y$ component there.\n"
msgstr "Mula sa commutator bounds patungo sa bounds sa backpropagated observable: kung ang observable ay commute sa isang $Z$ error sa isang qubit, hindi ito maaaring magkaroon ng malaking $X$ o $Y$ component doon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the bounds on the backpropagated observable to the commutator bounds: if the observable has little $X$ and $Y$ component on a qubit, then it must almost commute with $Z$ there.\n"
msgstr "Mula sa bounds sa backpropagated observable patungo sa commutator bounds: kung ang observable ay may kaunting $X$ at $Y$ component sa isang qubit, dapat itong halos commute sa $Z$ doon.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-inspection-1}"
msgstr "Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-inspection-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In principle, this tightening provides a smoother transition between the computed bounds and the trivial bounds assigned to the layers beyond the timeout. In this example the effect is barely visible, because the lightcones have already spread to the edges of the circuit by the time the timeout is reached.\n"
msgstr "Sa prinsipyo, ang pagpapahigpit na ito ay nagbibigay ng mas maayos na transition sa pagitan ng nakalkulang bounds at ng trivial bounds na ibinigay sa mga layer lagpas sa timeout. Sa halimbawang ito, halos hindi makikita ang epekto, dahil ang mga lightcone ay kumalat na sa mga gilid ng circuit bago pa man maabot ang timeout.\n"

