# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process {#step-4-post-process}"
msgstr "Step 4: Post-process {#step-4-post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we calculate the final expectation value of interest by using `executor_expectation_values`, we implement a few post-processing techniques to help ensure we obtain the highest-quality results possible. First, we apply our [twirled readout error extinction (TREX)](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex), which accounts for any errors occurring during the readout process. Then, we fix errors due to non-Markovian noise on our Heron backends by using a post-selection method. This method measures active and spectator qubits, then applies a slow rotation to each qubit, and then measures again. In instances where the two measurements do not confirm a flipped qubit as expected, these shots are discarded by applying a `mask` from the `PostSelector`. Within the mask computation, a specific strategy can be set to filter based on single-qubit nodes or neighboring spectator edges, which can influence both the number of shots filtered out and the quality of the results.\n"
msgstr "Habang kinakalkula natin ang huling expectation value na gusto natin gamit ang `executor_expectation_values`, nag-iimplementa tayo ng ilang post-processing techniques upang matulungan tayong makakuha ng pinakamataas na kalidad ng resulta na posible. Una, inilalapat natin ang ating [twirled readout error extinction (TREX)](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex), na sumasaklaw sa anumang mga error na nangyayari habang readout process. Pagkatapos, itinatama natin ang mga error dulot ng non-Markovian noise sa ating mga Heron backend gamit ang isang post-selection method. Sinusukat ng method na ito ang active at spectator qubits, pagkatapos ay naglalapat ng mabagal na rotation sa bawat qubit, at sinusukat muli. Sa mga pagkakataong hindi kinukumpirma ng dalawang measurement ang isang flipped qubit gaya ng inaasahan, itinatapon ang mga shot na ito sa pamamagitan ng paglalapat ng `mask` mula sa `PostSelector`. Sa loob ng mask computation, maaaring itakda ang isang specific na strategy upang mag-filter batay sa single-qubit nodes o neighboring spectator edges, na maaaring makaapekto sa parehong bilang ng shots na naifi-filter out at sa kalidad ng resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From examination of the experimental results, we can directly compare the behavior of the different approaches: PEC, PEC combined with SLC, and the unmitigated baseline. Some specific details to highlight:\n"
msgstr "Mula sa pagsusuri ng experimental results, direkta nating maikukumpara ang behavior ng iba't ibang approach: PEC, PEC na pinagsama sa SLC, at ang unmitigated baseline. Ilang specific na detalye na dapat itampok:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unmitigated result sits far outside the 10% bias band (near 0.35) and is unaffected by the number of randomizations.\n"
msgstr "Ang unmitigated result ay nasa malayo sa 10% bias band (malapit sa 0.35) at hindi apektado ng bilang ng randomizations.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "On this device, full PEC carries a sampling overhead of $\\gamma^2 \\approx 1.6\\times10^2$. After large early swings, the plain-PEC estimate recovers the signal and settles around 1.1, slightly overshooting the exact value. Note that the 10% bias band applies only to the PEC+SLC estimator: plain PEC is in principle unbiased, so this residual deviation is not covered by a bias guarantee but instead reflects statistical fluctuations and imperfections in the learned noise model, which is reasonable at this problem size.\n"
msgstr "Sa device na ito, ang full PEC ay may sampling overhead na $\\gamma^2 \\approx 1.6\\times10^2$. Pagkatapos ng malalaking maagang pagbabago, nababawi ng plain-PEC estimate ang signal at nananatili sa paligid ng 1.1, bahagyang lumalampas sa eksaktong value. Tandaan na ang 10% bias band ay para lamang sa PEC+SLC estimator: ang plain PEC ay sa prinsipyo ay unbiased, kaya ang natitirang deviation na ito ay hindi saklaw ng isang bias guarantee kundi nagpapakita ng statistical fluctuations at mga kakulangan sa learned noise model, na makatwiran sa laki ng problemang ito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "SLC reduces the overhead a further ~3.4-fold (to $\\gamma^2 \\approx 48$, for a residual-bias bound of about 10%). PEC+SLC also fluctuates strongly at few randomizations, initially even reaching into the unphysical region, but its estimate converges steadily onto the exact value, settling near 1.0 well inside the band. It matches or exceeds the accuracy of plain PEC at roughly a third of the sampling cost, demonstrating the benefit of lightcone shading.\n"
msgstr "Pinapaliit ng SLC ang overhead ng karagdagang ~3.4 beses (sa $\\gamma^2 \\approx 48$, para sa residual-bias bound na humigit-kumulang 10%). Ang PEC+SLC ay lumulukso rin nang malaki sa kaunting randomizations, unang umaabot pa nga sa unphysical region, ngunit ang estimate nito ay unti-unting nagko-converge patungo sa eksaktong value, nananatili malapit sa 1.0 nang maayos sa loob ng band. Tinutumbasan o hinihigitan nito ang accuracy ng plain PEC sa halos ikatlo ng sampling cost, na nagpapakita ng benepisyo ng lightcone shading.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error bars of both mitigated estimates contract as randomizations accumulate; at a fixed number of randomizations, the PEC+SLC estimator has the smaller statistical variance, consistent with its smaller $\\gamma^2$.\n"
msgstr "Ang error bars ng parehong mitigated estimates ay lumiliit habang naipon ang randomizations; sa fixed na bilang ng randomizations, ang PEC+SLC estimator ay may mas maliit na statistical variance, na naaayon sa mas maliit nitong $\\gamma^2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the learned noise rates (and therefore the overheads and mitigated estimates) depend on the backend and its calibration at the time of execution, so rerunning this notebook can produce quantitatively different values.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang learned noise rates (at kaya rin ang overheads at mitigated estimates) ay nakadepende sa backend at sa calibration nito sa oras ng execution, kaya ang muling pagpapatakbo ng notebook na ito ay maaaring makagawa ng mga quantitatively na ibang halaga.\n"

